* Fri Oct 09 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.5.0-1
- New name SailToken, as the earlier name is reserved in the Jolla Store
- The app keeps its file in a new folder of its own: add the file again
  from a saved copy, then set up the sync and the order of the accounts
  again

* Fri Oct 09 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.4.0-1
- Move an account to any place in the list with two taps; the order is
  kept in the file and survives the sync
- The icon has the same blue as SailVault's

* Thu Oct 08 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.3.0-1
- Sync with your own Nextcloud while the app runs; changes on the phone
  and on the computer are merged as KeePassXC merges them
- Merge a copy of the file from Documents or Downloads
- A warning when a file brings passwords without a one-time code, which
  belong in the password manager; the list marks such entries
- Empty the recycle bin in the settings, where deleted accounts kept
  their secrets
- New permission: Internet, for the Nextcloud sync

* Thu Oct 08 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.2.0-1
- Add a file from KeePassXC from Documents or Downloads, with or without
  a key file; a KDBX 3.1 file is stored as KDBX 4 with Argon2id
- Save a copy for the computer and delete the file in the settings
- Security review of 0.1.0: backups and folders owner-only, a lock
  during a save hides the codes at once, unusual secrets are read as
  strictly as KeePassXC reads them
- New permissions: Documents and Downloads, for adding a file and saving
  a copy

* Thu Oct 08 2026 Tobias Kaminski <instance_maintainer@protonmail.com> - 0.1.0-1
- First release: TOTP codes in an encrypted KeePass-compatible file of
  their own, apart from the password manager
- Add accounts by scanning a QR code or by typing the secret
- Same codes as KeePassXC for SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-512 and Steam Guard
- Copy with a tap; the clipboard is cleared after 30 seconds
- Locks after 2 minutes without use and 30 seconds in the background;
  every change is saved with three backups
